#
# .gitignore — Files Git must never track
# 2026-05-21
#
# Single source of truth for everything excluded from version
# control. Organized by concern; new patterns land in their section.
#
# Guidelines:
#   package-lock.json + templates/ are COMMITTED (CI + tarball)
#   .env.example is the only tracked env file (when present)

# ── Node / build / cache ─────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
dist/
build/
.cache/
.parcel-cache/
.turbo/
.eslintcache
.prettiercache
*.tsbuildinfo

# ── Logs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

# ── Test / coverage / reports ────────────────────────────────
coverage/
.nyc_output/
*.lcov
reports/

# ── Environment / secrets ────────────────────────────────────
# Real values live only on the contributor's machine.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
.env.*
# Tracked template (when present)
!.env.example

# Hard ban on common secret-file extensions — never commit
# these even accidentally. Add a specific pattern here if you
# ever need to intentionally commit an encrypted variant.
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.cert
*.pfx
*.p12
*.gpg
*.jks
*.keystore
*.token
*.secret
.htpasswd
.npmrc
.yarnrc
id_rsa
id_rsa.*
id_dsa
id_dsa.*
id_ed25519
id_ed25519.*
known_hosts
secrets/
credentials/
.secrets/
.aws/
.gcloud/
.ssh/
auth.json

# Generic database / SQL dumps — should never live in the repo.
*.sqlite
*.db
*.sql

# ── Editor swap files ────────────────────────────────────────
*.swp
*.swo
*~
\#*\#
.\#*

# ── OS junk ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
.fseventsd
.DocumentRevisions-V100
.TemporaryItems
.VolumeIcon.icns
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
ehthumbs_vista.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# ── Temp / backup ────────────────────────────────────────────
*.bak
*.orig
*.tmp
*.temp
tmp/
temp/
.temp/

# ── Local-only contributor files ─────────────────────────────
# Clipboard buffers for the most recent generated commit / PR
# text — overwritten in place every time new text is produced.
# COMMIT.md is the same thing under the extension the tooling
# actually writes; it holds prepared commit text, never code.
COMMIT.org
COMMIT.md
PR.org

# ── AI agent working directories ─────────────────────────────
# Session state, plans and transcripts belonging to a single
# contributor's tooling. Never part of the library or tarball.
.claude/
.shipwright/*.local.*

# NOTE: images/ and nodes/ were removed here at v1.1.0. They were
# an author's local sandbox that the TEST SUITE read from while
# being gitignored, so a fresh clone could not run the tests. The
# two fixtures the suite needed now live in tests/fixtures/.
